      "EntityImageNote still emits `data-qualified-name` from `getEntity().getQuark().getQualifiedName()`, while `Quark#getQualifiedName()` preserves the plasma separator and the SVG writer later translates each punctuation character independently."
    ],
    "rust": [
      "The parser path from 842f8604 remains intact: `push_note` stores `note.id` from `resolve_quark_path(alias, QuarkLookup::CurrentContext)` and registers that path in `note_by_path`.",
      "Relationship materialization still reuses named-note endpoints through `note_by_path` before entity/package fallback, which prevents the old phantom-class divergence.",
      "The follow-up implementation in `note_qualified_name` now prefers `note.id` and feeds the complete canonical identity through `translate_qualified_name(id)`, matching the Java `EntityImageNote` projection instead of reconstructing owner plus leaf."
    ]
  },
